    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Christian Yelich** (74.33) and **Caleb Durbin** (71.72). **Christian Yelich** is the anchor of the lineup; he benefits from a premier matchup against a hittable right-hander in Singer and a top-of-the-order boost that maximizes his volume. Meanwhile, **Caleb Durbin** remains a priority start due to the scarcity of stolen bases; his favorable park factors and the exploitable xERA of Feltner make him a high-efficiency play. **Junior Caminero** (70.91) also earns a premium spot as he looks to capitalize on a mid-rotation matchup against Wacha, with the lineup optimization favoring his current power-speed profile over more static depth pieces.\n\nWhile the core is set, we must note the high-stress matchup for **Yordan Alvarez** (61.66). Despite an elite xwOBA of 0.447, he faces the formidable Cease (xERA 3.15), which significantly suppresses his ceiling relative to his usual output. Conversely, **Lars Nootbaar** (65.90) thrives as our most underrated play, bolstered by a juicy matchup against Kelly and strong internal platoon metrics. On the bench, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** was the clear favorite for an OF slot, but he remains locked out due to today's rainout. No other bench candidates, including **Nelson Velazquez**, **Gary Sanchez**, or **Luke Raley**, crossed the 40-point threshold, leaving our prospect depth\u2014**Hyeseong Kim**, **Rece Hinds**, **Zac Veen**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Jose Fernandez**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez**\u2014safely stashed to preserve our season-long game caps. We are monitoring **Dillon Dingler** closely; while his 48.54 score is acceptable, he faces the tough arm of Cole, requiring us to keep a close eye on early-game performance to ensure he hits his projected floor.",
